Export newimage's euclideanDistanceTransform overloads from the shared library.

edt.cc force-instantiates these via the edtInstantiate() helper, but that
helper is marked __attribute__((visibility("hidden"))). Hidden visibility is
only honoured for static linking; in a shared libfsl-newimage.so the symbols
are not exported, so external consumers that link the .so (avwutils'
distancemap) fail with 'undefined reference to euclideanDistanceTransform'.
Add default-visibility explicit instantiation definitions (mirroring the
sparseInterpolate instantiation immediately above) so they are exported.

--- a/edt.cc
+++ b/edt.cc
@@ -146,4 +146,15 @@
   template auto __attribute__((visibility("hidden"))) edtInstantiate<char,short,int,float,double>();
 
   template volume<double> sparseInterpolate(const volume<double>& data, const volume<double>& weights, const double sigma);
-}
\ No newline at end of file
+
+  // Export the euclideanDistanceTransform overloads from the shared
+  // libfsl-newimage.so. The edtInstantiate() helper above forces
+  // instantiation but is marked visibility("hidden"), which only resolves
+  // for static linking; consumers that link the shared library (e.g.
+  // avwutils distancemap) need these exported with default visibility.
+  template volume<double> euclideanDistanceTransform<char>(const volume<char>&);
+  template volume<double> euclideanDistanceTransform<short>(const volume<short>&);
+  template volume<double> euclideanDistanceTransform<int>(const volume<int>&);
+  template volume<double> euclideanDistanceTransform<float>(const volume<float>&);
+  template volume<double> euclideanDistanceTransform<double>(const volume<double>&);
+}
